{
  "id": "ZEP.3",
  "number": "3",
  "bookId": "ZEP",
  "reference": "Zephaniah 3",
  "verseCount": 13,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "3",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ZEP 3"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "3",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jerusalem is doomed, that corrupt, rebellious city that oppresses its own people. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It has not listened to the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " or accepted his discipline. It has not put its trust in the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " or asked for his help. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Its officials are like roaring lions; its judges are like hungry wolves, too greedy to leave a bone until morning. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The prophets are irresponsible and treacherous; the priests defile what is sacred, and twist the law of God to their own advantage. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " is still in the city; he does what is right and never what is wrong. Every morning without fail, he brings justice to his people. And yet the unrighteous people there keep on doing wrong and are not ashamed.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " says, “I have wiped out whole nations; I have destroyed their cities and left their walls and towers in ruins. The cities are deserted; the streets are empty — no one is left. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I thought that then my people would have reverence for me and accept my discipline, that they would never forget",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3.7",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Some ancient translations",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "they would never forget",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "their dwelling would not be cut off.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " the lesson I taught them. But soon they were behaving as badly as ever.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Just wait,” the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " says. “Wait for the day when I rise to accuse the nations. I have made up my mind to gather nations and kingdoms, in order to let them feel the force of my anger. The whole earth will be destroyed by the fire of my fury.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Then I will change the people of the nations, and they will pray to me alone and not to other gods. They will all obey me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Even from distant Ethiopia",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3.10",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Ethiopia",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": See Word List.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " my scattered people will bring offerings to me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "At that time you, my people, will no longer need to be ashamed that you rebelled against me. I will remove everyone who is proud and arrogant, and you will never again rebel against me on my sacred hill.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3.11",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "sacred hill",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": Mount Zion (see Zion in Word List).",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I will leave there a humble and lowly people, who will come to me for help. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 3:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "REV.14.5"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Rev 14.5",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The people of Israel who survive will do no wrong to anyone, tell no lies, nor try to deceive. They will be prosperous and secure, afraid of no one.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.3.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
